    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.748"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.82"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The variables and decisive outcomes are clear. Published measurements likely permit checks of some components, but no known unified open dataset covers individual culture, mutant grafts and phase entrainment across the stated vertebrate scope." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Compare single-cell and collective presomitic-mesoderm oscillation traces, her1 dynamics in mutant hosts, and phase shifts after heterochronic grafting. The claim is supported if oscillation requires cell density and grafted cells converge on neighbour phase, and refuted by autonomous oscillation or persistent donor phase." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The three component experiments span species and laboratories.", "Single-cell movies and graft-level traces may exist only in supplements." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/levin-2024-collective-11--gpt--dataset-1> .
